  "data_abstract": "The W and Z boson production was measured via the muonic decay channel in p-Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm NN}}=5.02$ TeV at the Large Hadron Collider with the ALICE detector.\nThe measurement covers backward ($-4.46 < y_{\\rm cms} < -2.96$) and forward ($2.03 < y_{\\rm cms} < 3.53$) rapidity regions, corresponding to Pb-going and p-going directions, respectively.\nThe Z-boson production cross section, with dimuon invariant mass of $60<m_{\\mu\\mu}<120$ GeV/$c^2$ and muon transverse momentum ($p_{\\rm T}^\\mu$) larger than 20 GeV/$c$, is measured.\nThe production cross section and charge asymmetry of muons from W-boson decays with $p_{\\rm T}^\\mu>10$ GeV/$c$ are determined.\nThe W-boson production is also studied as a function of the collision centrality: the cross section of muons from W-boson decays is found to scale with the average number of binary nucleon-nucleon collisions within uncertainties.\n",
